In article <229@texsun.Central.Sun.COM> andy@misha.Central.Sun.COM () writes:
>I have been trying to get through a ghost level & keep adding more ghosts
>because every time I go down there,  I come across a pissed off shopkeeper
>(from a previously failed robbery attempt) who kills me immeadiately.  
>So why does the shopkeeper always assume that the person he comes across
>is the one who robbed him.  That person has long since been killed by the
>shopkeeper.  
>

Being able to re-roll a dead character is kind of paradoxical.  What did
you expect?  A rose by any other name might smell sweeter.

>Also, one more peeve.  I had a nice character going,  gray scale mail, & 
>more.  Killed an elf that was carrying a dead elf.  Since my god was pissed,
>I decided I needed to eat.  The computer asks if I want to eat one of the 
>2 dead elfes ?  Certainly,  oops... wrong one.  you die from tainted meat.
>I should know which one was fresh, since I just killed it.  How about
>a small change.  If there are two similar corpses,  when you eat one,
>default to the freshest.  
>

This feature is rotten.  I complained about this months ago.  The dev
team says that they average the ages when they merge corpses and that
this should not cause any problems.  If so then there is a bug in the
corpse tainting or corpse removal code (someone posted a bug-fix a
while back but I didn't pay much attention).  The dev team did not
list the bug among those fixed in pl8, so maybe they don't think it is
a bug.  Until the code is fixed, try this: name the live elf "fresh
meat".  Then when you kill him, he will be called "an elf corpse named
fresh meat" or something like that.  You get the idea.  Personally, I
think that the corpses should stay separate and that you should
recognize the freshest kill automatically.  The simplest way is to
leave him on top.

Beat death: copy your save files.

